## 3. Project record

`[Choice]` A project is an ordinary folder (exchangeable as a folder or a zip bundle — the formats are identical, the bundle just zips it):

```
myproject/
  project.json          # project record (below), schema-versioned
  notebooks/*.ipynb     # nbformat v4.5 documents [S1]
  transforms/*.sql      # named SQL transforms (DuckDB dialect) [Choice]
  data/                 # small curated files only; large sources stay in place
  runs/                 # one append-only event stream + artifacts per run (§5)
  manifest.lock         # stage/lock file, DVC-lock-shaped [S4; Inference]
  environment/requirements.lock   # resolved pins + hashes [S9; Choice]
  .locks/project.lock   # advisory lock file for concurrent open [Inference]
```

`project.json` fields `[Choice, grounded]`: `schema_version`; `datasets[]` — each `{name, path (relative), format, identity: {content_hash, size, recorded_at}, declared_schema or "untyped", import_options (delim/header/encoding/nullstr/…), read_mode: "zero-copy reference"}`; `environments[]` — `{python: "3.12", packages: [{name, version, hash}]}` `[S9]`; `stage_graph` mirroring `manifest.lock`; `created_by/opened_by` for humans only.

**No-copy import** `[Choice; grounded in S7]`: a dataset import registers *path + content hash + import options*; queries read the original file (DuckDB reads files in place; gzip/zstd auto-detected `[S7]`). A hash is computed at import (full read, streaming) and re-verified lazily on later sessions (cheap stat first, full re-hash on mismatch or on demand). Content identity is the hash, not the path: two analysts may keep the file at different paths and still share a manifest meaningfully. `[Inference]` Original files are opened read-only by the workspace; the product never writes to a registered source. `[Choice; brief constraint]`

**Preview semantics** `[Choice; brief constraint]`: a preview is the first K rows (or a stride sample) over the streaming reader, always labeled with `rows_shown` vs `rows_total: null|counted`, and a persistent UI marker "preview — not evidence about the full dataset". Counts that must be exact (row count, null counts per column for the contract) come from a separate full streaming pass, never extrapolated from the preview. `[Executed W3 part B]` demonstrates preview/total distinction; `[Inference]` for the full-scan being the only admissible proof.

