## 8. SQL boundary and the colleague

`[Choice]` Python notebooks are the authoring surface; **SQL is a first-class transform format** (`transforms/*.sql`) executed by the embedded engine over registered datasets. This gives the SQL colleague a real path — query the same datasets, produce outputs the same stage/lock system tracks — without the team building/maintaining a SQL kernel: the engine is in-process, the notebook stays Python (kernelspec `python3` `[S1, S2]`). Read-only exploration by the colleague runs against a copy of `project.json`'s dataset table; writes (transform outputs) are stages like any other, so they inherit hashing, invalidation, and quarantine. Other languages: not built (rejected alternative R2); the notebook format leaves room via kernelspec `[S1]`.

