## 11. Issue → fix → regression-test chain (required deep-dive)

**Chain: duckdb/duckdb PR #1015 — "CSV Loader would wrongly assume column with all sample values null to be Bool".** `[S5, S6]`
- *Failure:* the sniffer keeps a per-column candidate list and reduces it as sample rows arrive; a column whose sampled values were **all NULL** never reduced its list, so the last remaining candidate — BOOLEAN — won. The PR body: "Just defaulting this case to VARCHAR."
- *Fix (captured diff, merge commit `921d87713fd5052f5feed541cfdb2723b05a7a9e`, merged 2020-10-16):* in `SniffCSV`, add `LogicalType::SQLNULL` to the candidate list and, when a column's candidate list was never reduced (`size == full list`), force `VARCHAR`.
- *Regression tests (same PR):* new `test_auto_voter.test` (real 5,300-row voter TSV must read with count 5300); `test_sample_size.test` changed from `statement error` to `statement ok` on the sparse-column file `issue_811.csv` with expected `typeof` = INTEGER/VARCHAR/DATE/VARCHAR; `test_type_detection.test` case for integer-encoded booleans (INTEGER/BOOLEAN); test data added.
- *Version/branch applicability and evidence limits:* this is evidence about the recorded ref and 2020-era code (`buffered_csv_reader.cpp`). The CSV reader has since been rewritten (the open 2026 issue #25824 references `csv_scanner/sniffer/type_detection.cpp` `[S5]`), so the exact patch is not on current main; I did not capture a current-main equivalent fix. What transfers to the proposal is the *mechanism class*: inference over a sample leaves unconstrained columns, and unconstrained must mean VARCHAR/no-assert — corroborated by current docs (`auto_type_candidates` includes NULL with VARCHAR fallback `[S7]`) and reproduced in miniature by `[Executed W1]`. Additionally, the *related* sampling pitfall is **open, not fixed**: #25824 (created 2026-09-17, needs-triage, unclosed at capture) documents silent rounding/truncation past the sample across 1.1.3→main `[S5]` — an issue title and a merged patch elsewhere do not establish that *this* behavior is fixed, and it is reported unfixed; the design accordingly never trusts inferred types (§4-C1) and tracks the issue as lead L1.

A second, smaller observed failure — #15777, explicitly setting `dateformat='AUTO'` failing where auto-detection alone worked (closed 2025-02-06, "reproduced" label) `[S5]` — reinforces the same design rule (record the *detected* format as if declared; never re-sniff with different settings between import and replay), though its fix/PR was not captured, so no release-behavior claim is made for it.

